# Git

Do not commit unless the user asks. Do not push unless the user asks. Do not force-push. Do not skip hooks.

The commit hook is `.githooks/pre-commit`. It must call `.venv`'s Python by path. The editor's Git process resolves `python` to the Windows Store alias, which exits 9009. Do not point the hook at `python` or `uv` on PATH.

`results/`, `.venv/`, and secrets stay untracked. `uv.lock` is tracked. The jupytext `.py` notebook is the source of truth. The paired `.ipynb` is generated and stripped.

Do not commit dataset files. Record the license in an ADR before downloading.

Leave the GitHub remote alone until a push is requested.
